What this fork adds on top of upstream
--------------------------------------

* `packages/bundle/tui` — an interactive terminal profile (`dsh --profile tui`):
  a full-screen, alternate-buffer agent runner over `dsh-base` with no Host,
  HTTP, or browser layer. Includes the `tui-runner` plugin, a raw-mode line
  editor with slash-command autocomplete, a markdown renderer, inline diff
  rendering, multi-session switching (`/fork`, `/sessions`), and a session
  resume picker.
* `/setup` — an in-terminal wizard that configures and persists the API key,
  base URL, and model (`~/.dsh/.credentials.yaml` + `~/.dsh/settings.yaml`).
* Shell-tool rendering as a bordered panel (bash/pwsh/shell) with wrap-safe
  frame widths and frame-stripping on selection copy.
* Test assets under `scripts/`: `tui-unit.mts` (offline) and `tui-pty-e2e*.cjs`
  (pty end-to-end).

